WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
Such a sad midnight,

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
overflowing with love.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.970
kiiroi ringo o kajitteru

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.910
Gnawing at a yellow apple,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
kimi wa hitoshirezu otona ni naru

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
you secretly become an adult.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
tameiki iro shite mayoikomu

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
You sigh, having lost your way

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
ai o sagashite ikiteru

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
living in a search for love.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
suki yo tabun ne dakedo

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
Maybe I love you, but—

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
akai tsuki ga miteru

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
the red moon is watching,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
konna ni mo chikaku ni iru no ni

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
it waits nearby.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
Such a sad midnight.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.980
I can say love

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
It overflows with love.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.710
will you love me?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
tomadoi no hitomi no oku

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
Lost within your eyes,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
kokyuu o tomete

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
I stop breathing.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
kimi no ai o katachi ni

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
The shape of your love,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
mayonaka no taiyou

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
is like the midnight sun.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.230
I'm so sorry!

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.790
Could you check these right away, too?

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.740
Come on!

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.240
This is six days in a row! Six!

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.640
C-Can't I at least take a shower...?!

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.950
Here you go.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.450
I can't stand it anymore...!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.580
Seina-kun! Hurry back!

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:52.300
Introduction - Development - Conclusion

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.030
You appear rather exhausted, Seina-dono.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:58.600
I owe the honor to you...

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.870
You're still fine if you're energetic enough to be sarcastic.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:06.300
So, Seto-sama, where exactly might we be going?

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:11.010
Don't be so on edge. I'm going to show you something you'll like.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.240
Something we'll like?

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.580
I've mentioned fusing the Kamidake with a royal ship, haven't I?

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.420
Yes. You successfully linked it with the Mikagami the other day, so...

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.150
Oh!

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.190
Kiriko-san...

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.620
That's right.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.420
And this is Kiriko-chan's ship.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.480
The 2nd-generation Juraian ship, Mizuki!

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.170
This isn't a ship, it's just the core unit...

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:42.310
Actually, the term "royal ship" really refers to core units like this.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.800
What do you mean?

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:49.680
What's the matter, Seina-dono?

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.750
Eh? Oh, nothing...

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.080
Say...

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.380
Yes?

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.790
Has the unit's creation been completed?

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.390
All that's left is the fine-tuning.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:04.760
Really? In that case, why don't you give them a tour of the unit's interior?

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.130
Eh?!

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:07.560
Are you serious?!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.230
Why are you so surprised?

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.900
Because...

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:19.240
Royal ship units are kept top secret even from the galaxy's most elite...

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.380
They're not meant for people like us to enter...

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.180
Anybody can enter if the ship gives them permission.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.780
Is it really that simple?

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.310
How is Mizuki-chan doing?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.960
She says she wants us to come visit her.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.960
Oh, really? In that case...

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:42.870
Um...

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:43.770
What is it?

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.930
Um, Kiriko-sama...

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.640
What?!

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.710
I can act proper sometimes too, you know!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.750
You can call me how you normally do.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.520
I personally haven't changed at all, you see...

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.580
Oh, yeah?

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.320
It's just that I thought for sure that you had become especially elite!

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.320
Kiriko it is then! Kiriko! Kiriko!

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.020
On second thought, call me Kiriko-sama!

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.300
Welcome!

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.100
This is the bridge?! It's almost like a miniature garden!

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.690
This is the bridge...?

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:22.470
I've had the honor of being on Seto-sama's Mikagami once before,

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.380
but this ship's construction is completely different...

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.150
There is no "standard" royal tree unit.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:32.220
They're designed according to the preferences of the trees and the owners.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.310
And there we have Kiriko-chan's tree, Mizuki-chan!

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:44.860
I expected a royal tree to be giant or something, but it's actually so tiny...

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.660
Is this sapling the true form of the ships like the Mikagami,

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.200
which are said to be the strongest in the universe?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.270
Are you surprised?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.240
Say hello to everyone, Mizuki-chan.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.870
What the...?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.740
She's Amane.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.510
Amane...? Amane...! Amane!

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.180
What is this...?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:08.280
That tickles! OK, OK! That's enough!

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.790
Man, that really tickled...

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.560
A royal tree with a will of its own...

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.500
It was completely different from what I had imagined!

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.030
Lovely, wouldn't you agree?

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.840
That was almost like entertaining a playful little puppy!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.710
My back still sort of itches...

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.140
What is this place?!

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.010
What's the matter?!

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.510
Amazing!

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.150
Just as I thought...

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.810
This is the residential area.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.820
The inside of the Kamidake is amazing enough,

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.220
but is this really the inside of a ship?!

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.620
I've heard about this before, but actually seeing it boggles the mind...

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.530
This area is held within subspace by the tree's power.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:54.360
Thousands of people could live here and be completely self-sufficient!

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.200
So you've created a fully self-sustaining living environment here...

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:03.540
The units can create Light Hawk Wings of every field type,

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.380
as well as travel through both space and hyperspace.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.650
They also contain a nearly inexhaustible energy supply.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.880
Now do you understand why the core units themselves are the actual ships?

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:15.920
So then the exteriors are only for decorative purposes?

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.820
They're a kind of limiter.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.090
Limiter?

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.490
Royal ships' offensive capabilities are too powerful.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.830
They would be unusable if a single shot could blow away an entire planet.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.700
So that's why we use limiters.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:31.900
Couldn't you use these to rule the entire galaxy?!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.470
If you wanted to.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.440
But royal trees don't like fighting.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.180
I sort of got that impression.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.180
Not again...!

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.110
So she's just like Fuku-chan.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.620
The smell of the trees... what clean air this is!

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.520
This area could have been made even larger,

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.690
but it looks like Kiriko-chan held back for politeness' sake.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.190
She still hasn't even built a house.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.660
Eh? A house?!

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.200
Well, living here like this is perfectly fine and all,

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:05.040
but she will often be having guests over, so it would be nice to have one...

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.640
I want a HUGE one in here just for me!

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.070
Amane-san. That's not for you to...

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.080
I think I could have my castle built here!

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.880
Not you too, Neige-sama...!

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.680
And then I'd want a giant open-air bath, and a pool too!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.180
OK! I can agree to that!

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.380
What are you two saying?!

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:21.650
--Is something the matter?--A ski area!

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.090
--No, I just realized that Kiriko-san--Will you two stop that!

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:24.710
isn't back yet...

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:26.660
Fuku!

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.590
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.690
What do you think? Do you like them?

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.300
Really? That's good!

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:54.610
Sorry. I was just lost in thought. Don't worry.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.710
Fuku-chan!

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.370
Have you all finished looking around?

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:09.500
Are you by yourself, Fuku-chan?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.520
Hey! Fuku!

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:25.950
I forgot to mention that there are wild animals roaming around freely...

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.350
Would've been nice if you told us earlier!

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.700
Um...

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:43.370
What is it?

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.200
Those are Juraian clothes, aren't they?

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.170
That's right.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.970
They look... really good on you.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.940
T-Thank you...

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:55.310
But, well...

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:56.510
Eh?

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.650
No, it's nothing...

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.050
Oh...

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.650
We will now be conducting the fusion of the Kamidake

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:06.820
and the 2nd-generation royal ship Mizuki!

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.360
All hands, to your stations!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.390
That is all!

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.660
I anticipate good results from everyone's hard work!

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.500
Are you ready, Kiriko-chan? Fuku-chan?

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.400
Yes!

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.640
Mizuki-chan! We're starting now. Just relax.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.770
No anomalies with the Mizuki unit.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:27.240
Vibrations in the Kamidake's shell within acceptable parameters.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.980
30 until the shell achieves criticality.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.250
--20... 10...--Mizuki unit is stable.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.150
--5... 4... 3...--Checks show everything normal.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:35.220
2... 1...

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.380
Criticality!

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.060
The Kamidake's shell now disintegrating!

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:42.490
Brain waves stable and
--

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.860
The wave amplitudes have increased!

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:47.630
Energy output is escalating rapidly!

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.600
Mizuki unit is becoming unstable!

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.700
Number 2 has overloaded! Output is falling!

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.670
The Kamidake's shield output is dropping!

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:56.160
The living environment is beginning to shake!

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:01.510
Fuku-chan's pulse and breathing rates are both increasing!

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:04.510
If this shaking keeps up the dock itself won't last very long!

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:06.380
The energy fields are desynchronizing...

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.080
I can't maintain them!

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.720
The surge of mental waves has pushed them to their limits!

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.350
Cancel the--

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:13.190
Wait!

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:15.290
Mizuki! Fuku-chan!

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:16.950
Stop getting overexcited!

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.000
Oh...!

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.370
The dock almost fell apart there!

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.170
Both ships appear to be stable.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.040
I apologize, Seto-sama.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.440
My word...

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.680
I forgot that they are both still children!

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.250
Continue the fusion sequence!

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.280
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.620
Restarting fusion sequence!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.120
Mizuki unit repositioned.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.490
Unit implanted.

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.560
Beginning fusion reconstruction.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.670
All sequences complete!

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:06.040
Excellent work, you two!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.710
How is the link between Fuku-chan and Mizuki-chan doing?

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:11.050
There are no problems at all!

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:14.380
It appears it went smoother than the link with the Mikagami!

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:17.720
It's so stable there are almost no output variations at all!

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.750
Children can get along with others so easily...

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:26.860
If Fuku-chan and Mizuki-chan mature well...

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.900
...they just might surpass the 1st-generation ships!

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.900
Is it really all right to create such an excessively powerful ship?

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.500
What's wrong with it?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.900
They're both well-behaved children, after all...

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:37.670
And looking after them both is gonna be hard...

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.510
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:17.050
Kiriko-san...! Your clothes...

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.180
I think I prefer wearing these clothes during missions,

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.480
otherwise I can't seem to calm down...

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:28.630
Eh? You're coming too, Seto-sama?!

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:31.030
But of course!

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:33.200
Oh, and it looked like they had a lot of free time on their hands,

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:35.530
so I brought some other possibly lucky people along!

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.970
The more the merrier, right?

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:39.500
You know I don't have any free time.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.490
Oh? Then you would rather go back and take care of more paperwork?

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:46.180
No! I hate those mountains of paperwork!

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.480
Airi-sama sure has it rough too...

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.010
Seina-chan!

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.750
It's good to see you again!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.720
Mitoto-san! It's good to see you again...

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:57.120
So nice! It's been so long since I did this!

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:00.180
Is my crew cut really that nice?

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:05.230
What happened, NB?! You're completely white!

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:08.330
My masculinity... is gone...

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.530
NB-sama!

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:15.000
Some things have come up at home so I have to go sort them out,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:19.440
but I'll come back soon, so you'll have to survive without me for a while.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.940
"Come back"?!

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:26.350
And I'll never forget that night for as long as I live!

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.350
Don't remind me!

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.950
See you later, NB-sama!

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.620
NB... Who was that...?

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.090
I didn't do it! It wasn't my idea!

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.650
She forced me to!

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.870
We're sorry for being late, Seto-sama!

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:46.640
What are you guys doing here?!

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:50.570
I asked them to serve as sub-operators for this strike mission.

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.540
I can handle it just fine by myself!

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.910
I asked them to come because I deemed it necessary...

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:59.420
Do you have any doubts about my judgment...?

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.320
Tactical systems are reading normal.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.420
Secondary systems are at 12%.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.420
Navigations systems show all green.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:10.090
Corrective program loaded.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:14.760
Control checks show main systems and subsystems at normal.

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:19.240
Here you are, Fuku-chan! A carrot!

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.700
Let's go eat it over there, okay?

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:24.070
Well? They're all rather proficient, wouldn't you say?

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:26.410
Y-Yeah... They're amazing...

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:28.710
To think they even know how to take care of Fuku-chan...

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:31.410
You regular members need to work hard so you don't get one-upped.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.850
We don't need you to tell us that.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.050
Well, now that everything has been said,

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:38.390
Let's go have a showdown with the Good Luck Ship!

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.360
Right!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:43.660
That's fine, but do you know where the Good Luck Ship is?

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.630
Come now, we have a natural pirate radar right here!

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.970
Ah!

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:53.200
I somehow don't like the way you all agree like that...

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.870
Launch the Kamidake!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.540
Whoa, already?!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.770
There's a huge energy signature in front of us!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.740
Oh, my...

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:06.480
Years of work by the Juraian Senate have suddenly been made useless...

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:09.720
Ryoko! Don't tell me that's...

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.290
Eh? No way!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:17.790
Yes. The center of Da Ruma: mobile planetary fortress "Great Daruma"!

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.400
Hey now. All of a sudden?

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.300
W-What?!

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.370
The Kamidake has appeared?!

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:27.040
What have you perimeter surveillance people been doing?!

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.340
Please forgive us.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:31.340
It came out of a long distance jump without warning...

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:33.980
I can only think that our location was somehow leaked to them.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.050
That's impossible!

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.720
The Kamidake? Lorelei Seina, huh?

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:41.050
You damn pest!

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:44.490
Use every resource at your disposal to destroy him!

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:50.860
That's the Da Ruma fortress which the GP and Jurai could never find?

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:57.270
Not even we leaders were allowed to know its course or location.

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:01.840
Oh! But I remember being there before...

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:03.400
You're an exception, Mitoto-sama!

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.010
--The Great Daruma is attacking! --No problems with the barrier!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:10.850
Enemy ships have launched!

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:14.680
Currently 200 ships and increasing!

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.650
So you want a fight, do you?

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:21.320
Allow me to show you the power of a 2nd-generation royal tree!

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.090
Here we go, Fuku-chan!

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:26.230
Um, Seto-sama...

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:27.960
Technically I'm the captain--

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.530
Do you suppose you could leave me in command of the attack?

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:31.070
Um...

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.040
You have nothing against that, do you?

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:34.670
No...

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:37.570
Commence attack at once!

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:40.040
When she gets like that there's no stopping her.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.350
Just sit back and watch.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.400
Alright...

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:49.850
What?!

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:53.090
The Great Daruma's being assaulted by the Kamidake?!

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:56.490
Yes! They are battling it out now as we speak.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:00.530
Realizing you cannot defeat me and going after the Great Daruma instead

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:02.700
is as cowardly as you can get, Seina Yamada!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.430
We're going to the president's aid!

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.100
Prepare for hyperspace jump!

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.330
We start attacking the instant we exit our jump!

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.160
Seina Yamada!

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.690
Prepare to meet your doom!

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:33.800
I, Seiryo Tennan, shall be the one who--

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.700
P-Please don't kill us!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.470
I'll give you everything in our cargo hold!

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:43.470
My grandson was just born and I haven't even held him once!

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:44.570
Please, I beg of you...!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.410
Seina!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:51.450
You haven't seen anything yet!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.020
Stop scampering around!

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.080
--She sounds like she's really enjoying this...--Concentrate all fire on those ships!

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.390
That's the kind of person she is...

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:59.990
There's nothing for us to do, so would you like some tea?

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:01.360
Oh, that sounds lovely!

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:04.960
What kind of snacks would you like with your tea, Seina-chan?

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:07.160
Are we really in the middle of a battle?

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.800
What are you doing?! Destroy them at once!

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.400
The enemy ship has deployed Light Hawk Wings!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.000
Its maneuverability is far too high as well...!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.070
I don't want to hear your crying!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.040
And where is the Unko?!

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:21.310
I just contacted it so it should be here any minute.

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:27.380
I refuse to let all that I have created here be crushed by a single boy!

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:28.610
Why?!

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:31.690
Why aren't we arriving at the Great Daruma?!

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:34.660
Could it be that we're too lucky...?

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:36.030
I see.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:39.730
Dump all the lucky objects we've got stored onboard! Hurry!

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.360
We're exiting our jump.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.300
What the...?!

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.640
There's a huge GP fleet in front of us!

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.540
Why?!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.940
Just attack back at them!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.810
We aren't hitting them! Not even one shot!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.150
Why?!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.150
Random jump!

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.680
Excuse me! It broke!

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.050
Why?!

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.490
Could it be because we just abandoned all those lucky objects...?

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.150
I see.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:31.500
Go!

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:36.950
Do whatever it takes to stop them!

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.790
I don't care if it means ramming the fortress into them!

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:40.190
Just destroy them!

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:41.950
B-But...

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:47.390
Hey! What happened?!

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:52.430
You're so good at this, Fuku-chan!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:58.270
It's all over.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:02.480
It's begun hasn't it? Seto-sama's "Genocide Dance"!

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:06.180
What do you think about using your usual Triple-Z?

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.430
The Great Daruma has been destroyed...!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.680
So refreshing!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.320
You did great! You're such a good girl!

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:41.680
Even though we expected to fight the Good Luck Ship...

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:45.790
...we wound up fighting the Great Daruma and crushing the pirate guild.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.460
It is a slightly complicated feeling, isn't it?

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:52.030
I would have enjoyed it even more though

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:54.000
if the people in charge hadn't mutinied and surrendered to me.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:57.900
But thanks to them there was almost no resistance

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.670
so we were able to capture Da Ruma without anyone getting hurt.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.940
We caught them all in one fell swoop!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.880
You four did well too. I appreciate your hard work.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:09.650
No, we would do anything for Seina-senpai...

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.670
Now, now...

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.650
Come to think of it, where is Seina-sama...?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:19.520
Listen! I leapt into the world of piracy with just me and a single ship,

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:25.030
and only after I prevailed through countless battles and hardships

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:27.830
was I able to create the Da Ruma pirate guild!

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:31.870
That was the first step to the establishment of my empire!

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.540
I see...

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:37.500
To think that I would lose it all in this manner...!

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.380
I'm sorry.

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.980
I understand! I understand, Mister!

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:48.380
I understand all too well the sadness of a man who has lost everything!

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.690
You mean we're both in the same boat?!

00:21:50.690 --> 00:21:53.290
Of course, Da Ruma-san...

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.780
Roundy...

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.500
Curse you...!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:04.600
Curse you, Seina Yamada!

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:09.160
I will avenge the president! This I swear to you!

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:27.020
You're the worst, most hopeless,most unlucky boy in all of space...

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:34.890
Even against your will... (You fail.)

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.700
Even when you're gentle... (You're extremely clumsy.)

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:41.200
With too much fighting spirit, in vain, it's all coming to nothing...

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:44.190
You're gonna fail.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:48.040
Carefully... (So irritating!)

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.040
Or with violence... (Ow! Quit it!)

00:22:50.040 --> 00:23:01.110
You're the worst and most hopeless... you're a lost cause.

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:10.830
You're the worst and the most hopeless...

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:15.170
You're an unlucky boy...

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:20.510
But, any way, I'm with you.

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:25.670
So, more and more, keep on doing what you do!

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:34.650
Space is safe now that the Da Ruma pirate guild has been destroyed.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:37.180
But the problem really isn't that simple.

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:39.690
It seems the Good Luck Ship is still alive and kicking.

00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:40.890
So Seto-sama has come up with a plan...

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:42.600
Letter of Challenge

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:43.720
Next time on Tenchi Muyo GXP!

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:45.400
Showdown Between Good Luck and Bad Luck
